A||||12||Simple Fiero||How to remove a gopher||||1||
Z||000000||Simple Fiero||07-04-2001||02:09 AM||||Hello, not many of you know me, I am new here (DUH!)<BR>So I bought my first fiero today an 88 SC I was so happy and proud, and went to gas it up and climbed back in and the gas gauge doesn't work, no problem, I also find out that it doesn't have a key for the door again NO PROBLEM! I go to the lock smith to get one.<BR>I go home do some things around the house around 5 there is a knock at my door and it is the manager for my building, "Umm" he says nervously, and I can tell that something is wrong with my new baby. " I need you to bring your car keys down to the garage" Whew I think at least it ain't banged up. I ask "What's up", "There is a gopher under your car." " A WHAT?" I respond. So we go under and there it is sitting in one of my light bays a fricking gopher. we move the light and he jumps off and runs and jumps on my engine bay then runs and hides in one of the shock towers. We tried for like 4 hrs to get rid of him, but that is not the worst. I drive all the way to the store go in come out and he is sitting under the car just chillin. SO I think hey I will phone the Society for the Prevention of Cruelity to Animals (SPCA).<BR>And I told by some mean nasty phone person because it is a gopher they are considered a pest and there is nothing they can do. (JERKS)So I drive home and park outside in the vistor parking with it unlocked(I have theft insurance)cause I have no door key for it. And I belive the little bugger is still under there but I can't prove it. Damn I was mad, but now I find it humourous, but I am still slightly mad. So my question is how to remove a gopher(he looks like the one on caddyshack, wierd). But I still love my car, yippy!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||07-04-2001||02:14 AM||||You might try capsicum pepper spray (not Mace). It hurts like the dickens, but shouldn't harm him.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroSTETZ||07-04-2001||02:14 AM||||borrow a pellet gun to kill it, or get a paintball gun and shoot it with a wet cotton ball to knock it away from the car (used that on a neghbors cat who used to climb on my roof and pee on my window - yucky!)||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrgone||07-04-2001||02:37 AM||||strap a bra on your car and drive through a field of thorns. thattle learn `em!||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||07-04-2001||02:39 AM||||Call the SPCA again tomorrow and tell them it's a real ugly kitten.<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||overlord||07-04-2001||02:50 AM||||just trap it<BR>its gotta eat some time.||||reg||1
Z||000006||camaro2fiero||07-04-2001||03:16 AM||||A Gopher with class. He chose a Fiero with all the other cars around.Dont kill him , he aint gonna piss on the windows.Good Luck||||reg||7
Z||000007||rockcrawl||07-04-2001||08:59 AM||||I've had the same problem, but around here we call them ground hogs. I opened the trunk on my GT and the bastard was sitting on top of the trans! Scared the hell out of me! He ran down underneath and he just wouldn't come out. Apparently they like the taste of the grease and road salt that's all over the car. I could actually see where he had been scraping the grease off with his teeth.<P>Around here we just blast them with a rifle, but you gotta get them away from the car first. ||||reg||7
Z||000008||Oreif||07-04-2001||09:05 AM||||Go to a carwash with the undercarriage sprayers.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000009||p4n1c||07-04-2001||09:13 AM||||Just watch Caddyshack.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Use a fire hose, sniper rifle and plastique.||||reg||12
